    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "AIR PORT FILE.\nCITY OF SAN MATEO, CALIFORNIA,\nOffice of City Clerk\nSeptember 8, 1926.\nMAYOR JAMES ROLPH,\nJhe, and\nBOARD OF SUPERVISORS,\nSan Francisco, California.\nDear Sirs:\nPursuant to resolution of the City Council of San Mateo,\nthe undersigned as Mayor of the City, urges your serious considera-\ntion of the proposed aviation field immediately adjoining San Mateo\non the south for the use oi San Francisco as a Municipal Aviation\nField.\nOur consideration of the matter convinces us that the proposed\nsite has many advantages which makes it far superior to any of the\nother proposed sites on the peninsula.\nWith an area of Tive hundred acres available, with a length of\nover a mile and a half and a breadth of practically a mile, and with\nan absolutely level surface, the landing and take-off possibilities\nare unexcelled.\nThe proposed site is located between the leslie and Beresford\nstations on the main line of the Southern Pacific Railway, with a\ntrain service in excess of filty trains per day, and on the lain\nState Highway leading from San Francisco to San Jase.\nThe climatic and air conditions are extraordinarily good and\na portion of the proposed site has been used as an aviation field\nfor a number of years.\nAviators inform us that absence of fog and\nwind make it possible\nto land on this site at any and all times,\nwhich would unquestionably offset the time consumed by\nthe addi-\ntional distance from San Francisco.\nThis tield is immediately available and without grading or\nother improvement could be used immediately for aviation purposes.\nIt is also my understanding that the title to the property is in\nsuch a condition that\nthe site can be immediately secured at a very\nressonable price.\nThe proposed site is within a very short distance of the City\nof San Mateo, which has under contemplation the annexation of the\nproperty immediately adjoining the proposed site, and so far as the",
      "Board of Supervisors\nSeptember 8, 1926\npage 2.\nCity of San lateo can go in extending the customary courtesies between\ncities, it will do so in this instance for San Francisco in the way\nof police protection, etc. that may be required.\nWe urge your serious and immediate consideration of this\nproposed site.\nRespectfully yours,\nFREDERICK J. SMITH\nMayor of the City of San Mateo.\n650.810\n600-2"
    ],
